# Clarity Knowledge Wiki (OKF) — source of truth

The OKF knowledge wiki at `okf/` is the **canonical source for Clarity domain knowledge** — business rules, domain concepts, and data architecture. It follows the Open Knowledge Format v0.1 and the Karpathy LLM-Wiki pattern.

## What to do

- **Read the wiki first.** Before working on Clarity, read `okf/index.md`. Before any data-touching work (queries, models, widgets, migrations), read `okf/concepts/data-architecture.md` — Clarity uses PostgreSQL for writes and ClickHouse for analytics, and the two are frequently confused.
- **Follow `okf/CONTRIBUTING.md`** for ingest, query, lint, skill/planning integration, direct-maintenance chat workflows (`lint the wiki`, `update wiki from <source>`, `evaluate wiki against code`, `wiki status`), and the cross-repo search procedure.
- **Use the wiki for planning.** When running skills (brainstorming, design-review, planning) or producing planning/implementation docs in `docs/investigations/`, read the relevant concept pages first and cross-link them from the artifact.

## Source of truth ordering

When guidance conflicts, trust sources in this order:

1. **`okf/` (this wiki)** — canonical for **domain knowledge** (business rules, domain concepts, data architecture, engineering patterns, cross-repo registry).
2. **Code** under `app/`, `config/`, `database/`, `tests/` + `composer.json`/`package.json` — authoritative for **executable behavior**; wins over the wiki on code conflicts.
3. `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.

The legacy `.claude/docs/`, `.claude/skills/` knowledge companions, and `.serena/memories/` have been migrated into this wiki and deleted — do not look for them.

## Cross-repo awareness

When a question or plan may span other repositories, consult `okf/concepts/repositories.md` for the sibling-repo registry and search only the permitted surfaces, citing the source repo for any finding.
